  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The doppler effect's removal in Unity 2017 was apparently intentional, as indicated in this canny post: https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/doppler-on-audio-sources-no-longer-works\n\nThe doppler effect, when used right, can add a lot of interesting depth to audio, especially in worlds. It's a native Unity feature that does not appear to be harmful. I would like to see it re-added.\n\nIf newbie-friendliness is a concern, why not add an editor script to the SDK that sets the default doppler level to 0?",
